metrics=[('Cold open → full ready, ms','coldOpenToFullReadyMs',1),('Ensure / replay, ms','ensureReplayMs',1),('First full read, ms','firstFullReadMs',1),('Repeated full read, ms','repeatFullRead',1),('Single write, ms','singleWrite',1),('Batch 20, ms','batch20',1),('Upload, ms','upload',1),('Single ACK, ms','singleAck',1),('ACK-through, ms','ackThrough',1),('Compaction, ms','compact',1),('Mixed 300 operations, s','mixedMs',1000),('Worker user CPU, s','cpuUserMs',1000),('Worker system CPU, s','cpuSystemMs',1000),('Peak RSS, MiB','peakRssBytes',1048576),('Sampled peak heap, MiB','peakHeap',1048576),('Process write_bytes, GiB','processWriteBytes',1073741824),('Closed disk family, MiB','closedDiskBytes',1048576)]
lines=['# SQLITE-INCR-R3 — '+a['delivery'],'','Production decision: **WAIT**. Existing PR #958 remains draft. This report separates bounded SQL correctness, R2 performance and Main performance. No production adapter, merge, release, shadow/dual write, pilot or migration.','',f"Sources: Main `{src['main']}`; compatible R2 `{src['r2']}`; measured code `{src['measurementCodeSha']}`; validation adapter/tests `{src['validationCodeSha']}`. Final integrated Main is recorded separately in source-identity.json: its entire server/runtime/dependency source is byte-identical to measurement Main; only Horizon UI/acceptance and fast-check selection changed. Final integrated tests are repeated. Final evidence-only delivery head and its real CI are linked in the sole final #952 comment.",'','| Decision | Result |','| --- | --- |',f"| Incremental SQL + preserved supported compatibility | {a['incrementalSqlAndCompatibility']} |",f"| R2 → R3 performance | {a['r2ToR3Performance']} |",f"| Main → R3 performance, 10k | {a['mainToR3Performance10k']} |",f"| Main → R3 performance, 200k | {a['mainToR3Performance200k']} |",'| Production adoption | WAIT |','',a['r2ToR3Reason'],'']
for name,title,labels in [('A','A — compatible pinned R2 SQLite → R3 SQLite',['r2','r3']),('B','B — current pinned Main JSON/WAL → R3 SQLite',['local','r3'])]:
 r=s.get(name,{})
 lines+=['## '+title,'',f"Three alternating pairs per completed size. Complete: **{r.get('complete',False)}**. Values below are medians of three trial values; within-trial API timings use medians of the retained raw observations. No three-point p95 claim.",'','| Metric | 1k | 10k |' if name=='A' else '| Metric | 10k | 200k |','| --- | ---: | ---: |']
 for label,key,scale in metrics:
  cells=[]
  for size in ([1000,10000] if name=='A' else [10000,200000]):
   groups=r.get('sizes',{}).get(str(size),{}).get('groups',{})
   if all(l in groups for l in labels):cells.append(' → '.join(f"{groups[l]['metrics'][key]['median']/scale:.3f}" for l in labels))
   else:cells.append('BLOCKED / incomplete')
  lines.append('| '+label+' | '+' | '.join(cells)+' |')
 lines+=['',f"[All raw observations]({name}/raw.json), [trial medians, paired deltas and all metrics](summary.json). Full state, every mutation/upload/ACK receipt and fresh-process reopen hashes match in every completed pair; business output also matches the existing independent oracle.",'']
lines+=['## Real SQL, rollback and compatibility','','TEMP SQL audit (outside benchmarks): a single patch at 20 rows changes **82 → 3 DML**, at 2000 rows **8002 → 3**. R3 touches one record, one event and envelope; zero unrelated record/event writes. Duplicate and repeated ACK no-op produce zero DML. Batch, delete, remote conflict/resolution, upload, ACK and ACK-through audit covered. [Final audit](audit-final.json), [tests](../../../../../scripts/prototypes/sqlite-decision-20261109/incremental-r3.test.cjs).','','All operations persist their actual changed record/event/envelope values atomically; native SQL ABORT rolls back partial batch and metadata. Existing receipt/owner/CAS/HLC/ACK assertions remain. Five failure/write/ACK/close/reopen resource cycles, two-handle visibility, caller isolation and SQLite-only fresh process checks pass. The event-only failure trigger additionally covers envelope INSERT for the valid envelope-only ACK-through path; no assertion was removed. WAL/FULL, busy timeout 5000, cache -8192, autocheckpoint 256 unchanged.','','## A/A and unclosed gates','','Three controlled A/A pairs at each existing 1k/10k fixture use the identical final worker. Signed deltas and all samples: [1k](AA-small/raw.json), [10k](AA/raw.json), [summary](summary.json). No blanket percentage tolerance or mere broad min/max waiver. The earlier repeatable get regression was fixed before final acceptance; historical samples stay under read-regression-2581c655. The final small filter gate remains explicitly open as explained above.','','Full-state SQL materialization and envelope serialization remain expensive; ordinary DML reduction is not an end-to-end production acceptance. Each API sample records SQL all() rows/time and envelope serialization size/time. Compaction is separate; its ledger/envelope growth is retained. Native /proc process write_bytes includes query/sort temporary files, not commit-only bytes. Instantaneous DB/WAL/SHM/recovery sizes are not cumulative writes. CPU/event-loop worker totals include harness/oracle overhead; per-API timing excludes separate full canonical hashes. Fresh process uses warm OS cache, not OS-cache-cold. Equivalent automatic backup/retention/rollback and platform/power-loss guarantees are not established; disk-family numbers do not close those gates.','','## Validation and provenance','']
for name,v in s['validation'].items():lines.append(f"- {name}: {v.get('tests')} tests, {v.get('pass')} PASS / {v.get('fail')} FAIL / {v.get('skipped')} SKIP / {v.get('cancelled')} CANCEL.")
lines+=['','Full standard npm runner: 1335 files, 10 uninterrupted batches, default concurrency=4; official targeted runtime Electron 44.3.0 / Node 24.20.0 / SQLite 3.53.4; standard npm host Node 24.19.0. i18n 0 new / 0 baseline missing; existing 23 release-note records valid. New note/PNG N/A: product/CI sources equal Main. No other candidate branch, package/lock, production engine or threshold changes.','','Official archive checksum, cgroup/CPU/overlay environment, protected tree equality and file hashes: [source identity](source-identity.json). [Pre-implementation budgets](plan.md), [reproduction commands](commands.md), [critical review](review.md), [all prior failed/stopped attempts](attempts.json). The copied conversation’s unpushed eec7896e source was unavailable; no claimed prior R3 measurements were adopted. Final validation/measurement identities are explicit; later evidence commits do not change runtime sources.','','Final single report: #952 [SQLITE-INCR-R3]. PR #958 stays draft; Main merge, TEST/STABLE, publication, shadow/dual-write, pilot, migration, branch deletion and issue closure are not performed.']
